WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.400
SUBJECT MXene · PROMISING ENERGY-STORAGE MATERIAL · IN-BODY SAFETY: ???

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.400
MXene VOYAGE · A FANTASTIC NANO MISSION

3
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.000
WHAT IS MXene? A thin material that conducts like a metal

4
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.300
TESTED: MXene NANOSHEETS · IMAGINARY INSPECTORS · WHAT IS MXene? A thin material that conducts like a metal

5
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.000
IMAGINED TOUR: Rats received only MXene nanosheets · the device never went inside

6
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.900
MXene is a promising energy-storage material, but is it safe in the body? (IMAGINED TOUR: Rats received only MXene nanosheets · the device never went inside)

7
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.400
THE PROBLEM: Data on MXene toxicity in the body were limited and sometimes inconsistent

8
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.000
Same question. What was checked? (BEFORE | THIS WORK)

9
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.600
BEFORE: REPORT A · mice, IV injection No major inflammation / REPORT B · zebrafish Dose-dependent toxicity · Varied conditions, no multi-route assessment

10
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.400
THIS WORK: Dermal once, Oral 28 days, Intraperitoneal 28 days · 28-day groups: blood markers and five organ tissues (Liver, Heart, Kidney, Lung, Spleen)

11
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
BEFORE: DATA GAP (no multi-route assessment) | THIS WORK: 3 ROUTES TESTED (no major abnormalities at tested doses · some mild changes)

12
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.000
The same MXene nanosheets, device performance and material toxicity tested separately: Device performance electrochemistry outside the body / Material toxicity nanosheets given to SD rats · The finished device was not tested inside a body

13
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.700
(Before: gaps named in the paper's introduction · This work: what was tested (not a safety ranking)) In-body toxicity data: Before Limited, sometimes inconsistent | This work New toxicity data in SD rats · tested doses: no major abnormalities, some mild changes

14
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:21.900
Dosing routes: Before No multi-route assessment | This work Dermal, oral, intraperitoneal · dermal once (acute) · oral and intraperitoneal 28 days

15
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.400
Finished device MXene//AC: Areal capacitance 66.43 mF cm⁻² (at 0.5 mA cm⁻²) · Power density 2300 W kg⁻¹ (at 4 mA cm⁻²) · Capacitance retention ~95% (after 5,000 cycles)

16
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.400
SHOWN IN THE PAPER: Bent, or worn on a hand · device fixed at each angle / on the back of a hand: flat vs bent · Charge–discharge time: slight change at 30° · nearly the same at 60° and 90° · flat and bent hand nearly the same

17
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.000
OUTLOOK: Wearable electronics, and possibly energy storage for implantable devices · Safety of implanting the device and long-term safety still need study (paper)

18
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.000
MXene nanosheets, from energy storage to toxicity tests

19
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.600
Um... can we get un-shrunk now?
